WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.712
When we group by product, Spark must bring rows with the same product together.

00:00:04.712 --> 00:00:09.707
If those rows are spread across partitions, the engine needs a shuffle.

00:00:09.707 --> 00:00:15.762
This is why aggregation is not just a mathematical step.

00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:18.422
In distributed execution, it also has a data-movement cost.

00:00:18.422 --> 00:00:23.977
A shuffle moves data across executors so related keys end up together.

00:00:23.977 --> 00:00:30.147
GROUP BY, large joins, and global ORDER BY can trigger expensive shuffles.

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:36.827
In distributed systems, moving data is often more costly than evaluating the SQL expression itself,

00:00:36.827 --> 00:00:38.708
so plan around data movement.
